From: Jacob Cook <jacobmcook1984@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: rk817-charger: reject a boot counter below the voltage floor

Booting from the columb counter assumes it kept counting while the
system was off. On a GKD Pixel2 (4.35 V pack, fcc 1730 mAh) it came
back from more than four hours powered off 1.08 Ah lower than it went
in, with the pack still at 4.27 V open circuit:

  boot: counter 544036 uAh, saved soc 94480, fcc 1730 mAh, battery 4269990 uV

The saved soc and the battery voltage both put the pack near 95%; the
counter said 31% and was taken, and the device ran at 31% until a full
charge reset it. The BSP driver's halt test adopts the counter on the
same divergence, so it reproduces the same result.

On battery the load holds the terminal voltage below the open circuit
voltage, so the ocv table applied to the voltage read at probe is a
floor under the state of charge whatever happened while the system was
off. A counter more than a tenth of the pack below that floor cannot be
right; keep the saved soc, the last state the gauge tracked. The check
is skipped with a charger present, where the terminal voltage sits
above the open circuit voltage instead. Log OFF_CNT with the rest of
the boot line; the datasheet gives it no unit.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-5-fable
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
@@ -854,7 +854,7 @@
 {
 	struct rk808 *rk808 = charger->rk808;
 	u32 boot_charge_mah;
-	int ret, reg, tmp;
+	int ret, reg, tmp, off_min, bat_uv, boot_soc, floor_soc;
 	bool first_boot;
 	u8 bulk_reg[4];
 
@@ -912,18 +912,34 @@
 		regmap_bulk_read(rk808->regmap, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_Q_PRES_H3,
 				 bulk_reg, 4);
 		tmp = get_unaligned_be32(bulk_reg);
+		regmap_read(rk808->regmap, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_OFF_CNT, &off_min);
+		bat_uv = rk817_bat_voltage_uv(charger, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_BAT_VOL_H);
 		dev_info(charger->dev,
-			 "boot: counter %d uAh, saved soc %d, fcc %d mAh, battery %d uV\n",
+			 "boot: counter %d uAh, saved soc %d, fcc %d mAh, battery %d uV, off_cnt %d\n",
 			 tmp > 0 ? ADC_TO_CHARGE_UAH(tmp, charger->res_div) : 0,
-			 charger->soc, charger->fcc_mah,
-			 rk817_bat_voltage_uv(charger, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_BAT_VOL_H));
+			 charger->soc, charger->fcc_mah, bat_uv, off_min);
 		if (tmp > 0) {
 			boot_charge_mah = ADC_TO_CHARGE_UAH(tmp,
 							    charger->res_div) / 1000;
 			if (boot_charge_mah > charger->fcc_mah)
 				boot_charge_mah = charger->fcc_mah;
-			charger->soc = boot_charge_mah * 100000 /
-				       charger->fcc_mah;
+			boot_soc = boot_charge_mah * 100000 / charger->fcc_mah;
+
+			/*
+			 * On battery the load holds the terminal voltage below
+			 * the open circuit voltage, so the ocv table puts a
+			 * floor under the state of charge. A counter more than
+			 * a tenth of the pack below that floor lost its count;
+			 * the saved soc is the last state the gauge tracked.
+			 */
+			floor_soc = charger->plugged_in ? -1 :
+				power_supply_batinfo_ocv2cap(bat_info, bat_uv,
+							     20) * 1000;
+			if (boot_soc < floor_soc - 10000)
+				dev_info(charger->dev,
+					 "counter below the voltage floor, keeping saved soc\n");
+			else
+				charger->soc = boot_soc;
 		} else {
 			dev_info(charger->dev,
 				 "columb counter invalid, keeping saved soc\n");
